# Claude Code Configuration for TestRPGGame

## Session Tracking & Development Workflow

### IMPORTANT: Start Every Session Here
Before beginning any work, follow this workflow:

1. **Read DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md**
   - Review the most recent session to understand what was done
   - Check "Pending Tasks" section for prioritized work items
   - Review "Known Issues" for any blockers
   - Understand the current state of the project

2. **Verify Project Health**
   ```bash
   dotnet test  # All 86 tests should pass
   git status   # Check for uncommitted changes
   ```

3. **Start New Session Entry**
   - When beginning work, add a new session entry to `DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md`
   - Include: Date, context, and goals for this session
   - Use the existing format as a template

### Session Documentation Standards

#### During the Session
- Use the `TodoWrite` tool to track tasks in real-time
- Document completed tasks with:
  - What was changed (specific file references with line numbers)
  - Why it was changed (context and motivation)
  - How it works (technical implementation notes)
  - Test results and validation

#### End of Session Checklist
- [ ] Update `DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md`:
  - Add all completed tasks to current session
  - Update pending tasks with new items discovered
  - Add any new known issues
  - Write session summary with stats (files changed, tests passing, etc.)
- [ ] Run final tests: `dotnet test`
- [ ] Commit all changes with detailed message (see Git Commit Standards below)
- [ ] Verify all tests still pass after commit

### Quick Reference Files

- **DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md** - Complete session history and task tracking
- **SESSION_GUIDE.md** - Quick reference for commands and workflows
